    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get that it's supposed to be a compromise, but isn't that just a nice way of saying the rules only apply if they don't inconvenince the people who wrote them? like, when a superpower actually breaks a major treaty or ignores a court ruling, there's zero real consequence. doesn't that basically prove that \"accountability\" is just a theory that only applies to the countries that don't have any real leverage?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
