      "content": "thanks. but that \"diplomatic cost\" thing feels pretty weak when you realize the big players can just shrug it off or use their veto power to kill any real action. it feels like we're just kidding ourselves by calling it a \"mechanism to check power\" when it's clearly just a way to manage the fallout of hegemony. if the system can't actually stop a superpower from doing what it wants, isn't it basically just a legitimizing tool for the existing power structure rather than a way to change it?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
